[b]CyberTaxi version 7.30q - January 21, 2021 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] Meteor Showers weather was added in The Projects district (instead of Snow weather);
[*] Acid / Toxic Rains were added in The Park district (instead of standard Rain weather);
[*] redesigned Buzzsaw weapon mechanics;
[*] Buzzsaw weapon gets blood stains if you cut pedestrians or terrorists;
[*] Buzzsaw weapon makes scratchy noises and emits lots of sparks if you hit enemy cars;
[*] updated Buzzsaw sprites;
[*] Proton Nav-Sat weapon now destroys pedestrians and terrorists too, not only cars;
[*] Plasma bolts burn and melt pedestrians and terrorists instead of spilling blood;
[*] added some gloomy lights in the darkest spots and areas in The Downtown district;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/38802170/95a85a0e8912176a2825a65a534b00578ae8dfd6.png[/img]

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.28q - January 15, 2021 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] fixed the double destination spawns glitch; 
[*] fixed the wrong mission info/text bug which occurred from time to time;
[*] fixed some map mission markers;
[*] manual weather control added to the game (press "." key to change weather in game);
[*] fixed some minor glitches with various settings and options in the main menu;
[*] controls updated;
[*] changed positions of some turrets in The Downtown district;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.25q - January 10, 2021 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] picking up a customer pauses the game, pauses the timer and opens the map - you can use it for conversation freely; 
[*] you can exit the map by pressing ESC key or M key, also, activating map pauses the game;
[*] added new raindrop post-processing screen effects with refraction shaders (use Ultra Settings to activate them);
[*] added special main menu loader - important fix for all people who had the black screen issue;
[*] fixed an issue that caused the loaded game to display wrong color of health notification;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.23q - December 31, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] in order to exit any store you can also use the ESC key (you can pause the game by pressing the ESC key only while you're not in a shop);
[*] updated store sprites;
[*] updated The Projects map;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Happy New Year everybody! :)

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.21q - December 30, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] new trash and litter system - there is a plethora of garbage on the streets;
[*] many effects tweaked or enhanced to give better visual results;
[*] added a lot of new synth wave music to the game (thanks MIKE OST!);
[*] new options in the Main Menu - you can turn ON/OFF Antialiasing, Motion Blur, Lens Flares;
[*] added some skeletons in the cemetery area in The Park district;
[*] some terrorists are more diverse now in terms of appearance;
[*] polished some Main Menu items;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Remember to stay safe, especially in CyberTaxi.

[b]Winter Holidays[/b] have arrived to Hindenburg! Starting from today until 31st of December, you can witness some Christmas Trees in many places and find special collectibles. Also, snowy weather and blizzards will occur in every district in December and January. You can even find drunk Santa in every district and slay him to get $20! Damn! :3

[b]Find new winter presents / gifts collectibles[/b] scattered across every district in CyberTaxi in order to unlock the powerful and unique Proton Beam Nav-Sat weapon. Warning! Some presents were hidden carefully - you have to collect all of them (8 presents in at least one district in order to obtain the weapon). You may even have to search for secret areas...

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.19q - December 20-24, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] special Christmas Holidays event and special events system added, including drunk Santa;
[*] [b]ray tracing has been added to the game[/b] - use the high quality settings to activate it;
[*] cyberpunk-style lens flares and glare effects have been added to the game;
[*] pause feature was added to the game - use the Escape key to pause the game;
[*] while the game is paused you can access the map and talents freely;
[*] many objects, sprites and normal maps have been fixed and updated;
[*] fixed some lamps in The Downtown district;
[*] FSAA modified to provide better quality results;
[*] changed some features in the Main Menu;
[*] snow system added to the game (it will occur randomly even after the end of the event);
[*] fixed a bug which caused the weather to change dynamically in indoor areas;
[*] driving model updated;
[*] quality of many textures fixed;
[*] new visual quality presets added (High is default, use Ultra for Ray Tracing reflections);
[*] fixed rocket turrets in The Old Town (including the one that attacked you in Repairtec);
[*] the main conversation text in the map screen is instantly displayed (no type-writing anymore); 
[*] many other bugfixes.
[/list]

Have a lovely Winter Holidays! Regards! XOXO!
CyberTaxi Developers

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.05z - December 9, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]enemy cars are much easier to destroy now[/b] which provides more satisfaction;
[*] many normal maps fixed and updated, some effects will look better now;
[*] updated many sprites and weapon sprites;
[*] fixed many lights in The Downtown district;
[*] garbage textures updated;
[*] added some new content in the Main Menu;
[*] credits updated;
[*] driving model was slightly polished;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Remember to stay safe, especially in CyberTaxi.

[b]CyberTaxi version 7.03z - December 6, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] driving model has been enhanced, taxi is a bit faster and turns more easily;
[*] huge optimization of the game, it should work much faster now on most rigs and systems;
[*] fixed many sprites that contained some bugged alpha transparency;
[*] lots of minor tweaks in The Downtown and The Park districts;
[*] loading bars were added to the game;
[*] loading times should be shorter in most cases;
[*] pressing random buttons or mouse click won't crash the game while loading;
[*] added new ray-tracing semi-like materials;
[*] many fonts were fixed;
[*] mines can be destroyed now by shooting them;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Santa Claus has visited the world of CyberTaxi, but he got jammed somewhere. Can you find the Santa Claus? >.<"

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.49z - November 20, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] added brand new textures to the game and updated many normal maps;
[*] new starting location in The Downtown;
[*] some mines were updated - mines hidden under the ground were removed;
[*] fixed cab colors, they're more accurate now;
[*] additional optimization of shaders;
[*] weapon slots removed - instead you can quickly switch between obtained weapons;
[*] some weapon sprites have your cab color;
[*] fixed some trees in all districts;
[*] fixed some scaling issues of buildings in The Projects;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Remember to stay safe, especially in CyberTaxi.

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.45z - November 15, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] fixed a bug which triggered Cab crash damage sounds while using some weapons;
[*] fixed a bug which blocked some weapon bullets while driving fast and shooting - now you can drive at maximum speed and shoot without any problems;
[*] Gambricorp droids can be destroyed by using Buzzsaw from now on;
[*] weapons are more balanced now and shoot much faster;
[*] Buzzsaw was redesigned to be a more powerful weapon and has 400 ammo units as default (increased from 200 units, special talent will provide you with 600 ammo fuel oz units);
[*] Lightning Sword was also enhanced and has 400 ammo units as default;
[*] fixed a few objects and sprites in the Main Menu;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Remember to stay safe, especially in CyberTaxi.

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.42z - November 14, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*] new Flamethrower has been implemented;
[*] new Buzzsaw effects after attacking enemies - lots of sparks in case of enemy cars and many gibs in case of humanoids;
[*] Flamethrower and Buzzsaw weapon range increased - both weapons are much more effective now;
[*] fixed a few textures and sprites, including a new Kitty gadget model;
[*] many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.39z - November 8, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*]all missions in the Old Town have been fixed and tested;
[*]tutorial redesigned - instead of lame 2D boards you have some notifications while driving your taxi;
[*]fixed some spawners in all districts;
[*]fixed the column with flickering textures in Downtown;
[*]fixed cursor visibility issues;
[*]fixed some textures and sprites;
[*]updated position of a few UI elements in the Main Menu;
[*]loading times should work properly on most rigs now;
[*]EMP blasts of flying ships now correctly explode on the roads.
[/list]

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.28z - November 7, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*]fixed many items, turrets and positions of small objects in all districts;
[*]fixed double spawn issue;
[*]fixed problems with 'customer eject' function;
[*]new achievements added;
[*]cab is slightly faster now and engine has a bit more power;
[*]levels should load a bit faster;
[*]flying ships fixed and some of them launch EMP blasts.
[/list]

Important Note for NVIDIA Graphics Card Owners - we would like to inform you that after installing latest NVIDIA Experience Video Card drivers (or previous drivers) you may experience longer loading times in case of Main Menu and Downtown. We are working hard to fix that issue. Therefore, please wait a bit longer in case of black screen - the game will load the levels sooner or later.

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.25z - November 4, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*]all effects have been enhanced and increased (Bloom, SSAO, Grain);
[*]new Gore System was added to the game;
[*]fixed colliders of some objects;
[*]fixed some issues in the Downtown with train tracks;
[*]fixed fonts of secondary weapons;
[*]all maps finally fixed and show the exact positions of important objects;
[*]CyberTaxi has been updated to the newest stable version of the Unity engine;
[*]many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

Important Note for NVIDIA Graphics Card Owners - we would like to inform you that after installing latest NVIDIA Experience Video Card drivers (or previous drivers) you may experience longer loading times in case of Main Menu and Downtown. We are working hard to fix that issue. Therefore, please wait a bit longer in case of black screen - the game will load the levels sooner or later.

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.15z - November 3, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*]new tutorial features which explain main game mechanics;
[*]fixed colliders of garbage trucks;
[*]fixed some issues in first district, game should run a bit faster now;
[*]fixed issues with some sprites of secondary weapons;
[*]maps were updated;
[*]we have finally fixed that bloody map in the first district (sorry that it took us so much time);
[*]many minor bugfixes.
[/list]

[b]CyberTaxi version 6.14z - November 2, 2020 - Changelog[/b]:
[list]
[*]new compass in form of a miniradar has been added to the game - it works properly now;
[*]fixed issues with V-Sync, game should run much faster now on some rigs;
[*]fixed fonts and some settings options in the Main Menu;
[*]added new logos and emblems; 
[*]fixed maps and player markers;
[*]fixed some sprites;
[*]many other minor bugfixes.
[/list]
